{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2170-01-16 04:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I'm Dr. Lee, one of the surgery team doctors. You were admitted overnight due to ongoing nausea and trouble keeping food down after your gastric bypass."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2170-01-16 04:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been so nauseous. I can’t eat more than a few bites. I’ve been relying on the TPN through my central line."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2170-01-16 04:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Your history shows you had ulcers after the bypass, which are now healed, but the nausea and poor intake have continued. We’re concerned about malnutrition, which is why you’ve needed TPN."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2170-01-16 04:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right. I’ve lost a lot of weight. I just can’t tolerate eating. Is there anything we can do?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2170-01-16 04:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. The plan is to place a gastrostomy tube—what we call a G-tube—through your abdomen into your stomach. This will let us give you nutrition directly into your stomach instead of through your veins."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2170-01-16 04:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So, like a feeding tube? Will I still be able to eat by mouth at all?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2170-01-16 04:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s a feeding tube. We’ll start with tube feeds at night. Over time, you may still be able to eat small amounts by mouth, but the tube will make sure you get enough nutrition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2170-01-16 04:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And this is done with surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2170-01-16 04:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, a laparoscopic procedure—small incisions, camera-guided. It’s low risk, and we do it often for patients in your situation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2170-01-16 04:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. When would it happen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2170-01-16 04:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Later today. The OR schedule has you set for around noon. We’ll go over consent and prep you shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2170-01-16 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, it’s Dr. Lee again. You just came back from surgery. The G-tube was placed successfully—no complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2170-01-16 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, good. I didn’t feel anything—must’ve been out cold."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2170-01-16 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, general anesthesia. The tube is in the right spot. We’ll wait until tomorrow to start feeds, after we confirm placement with a contrast study."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2170-01-16 12:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Will it hurt when I start using it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2170-01-16 12:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You might feel some soreness around the site, like after any small surgery. But it shouldn’t be severe. We’ll manage pain with medication."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2170-01-17 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. I’m reviewing your imaging from last night. The gastrograffin study shows the G-tube is in the correct position in your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2170-01-17 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Does that mean we can start the feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2170-01-17 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Nutrition team is starting you on Fibersource HN through the tube at a low rate. We’ll increase it gradually."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2170-01-17 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my TPN? Will I still need that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2170-01-17 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve already stopped the TPN. The goal is to get you fully off it. The tube feeds will replace it over the next few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2170-01-17 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I never liked the central line. It felt like a constant reminder I wasn’t healing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2170-01-17 08:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. Once we confirm you’re doing well on tube feeds, we’ll remove the central line."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2170-01-17 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling? Any nausea or discomfort from the tube feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2170-01-17 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Actually, no. I don’t feel worse. Maybe a little full, but not sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2170-01-17 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. We’re keeping the rate low today, but tomorrow we’ll increase it. The goal is 80 cc per hour for 12 hours overnight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2170-01-17 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Overnight only? So I’m not hooked up all day?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2170-01-17 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, just overnight. That’s called cycled feeding. Gives your stomach a break during the day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2170-01-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re up to 80 cc/hr and tolerated it well last night. No issues with nausea or bloating?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2170-01-18 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, actually slept better. I didn’t wake up hungry or sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2170-01-18 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. That’s exactly what we want. We’re also going to remove your central line today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2170-01-18 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? That’s great. Is it safe to remove it now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2170-01-18 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’re stable, well-nourished from the feeds, and no longer need TPN. The interventional radiology team will remove it this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2170-01-18 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Your central line has been successfully removed. The site is clean, no bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2170-01-18 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t even feel it. I’m so glad it’s gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2170-01-18 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep the area covered for a day or two. You’re doing really well on the G-tube feeds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2170-01-18 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I try eating a little by mouth again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2170-01-18 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve started you on a stage V diet—full liquids. Things like broth, yogurt, protein shakes. We’ll see how you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2170-01-18 15:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had some apple juice earlier. No nausea. That’s a big improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2170-01-18 15:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. You’re off TPN, on full tube feeds, and tolerating oral intake. We’re looking at discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Today’s the day—we’re getting ready to send you home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? I feel ready, but I’m a little nervous about managing the tube at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Totally normal. A nurse will come to your home to help with the overnight feeds. And you’ll have detailed instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like how to check the tube before feeding?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You’ll use a syringe to check for residual—any leftover formula in the stomach. If it’s more than 50 ml, you’ll pause and call us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the dressing around the tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Wash with mild soap and water. Apply antibiotic ointment and a dry dressing until it stops draining. Once healed, you can leave it uncovered."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I keep taking the pantoprazole?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, once daily. It helps prevent ulcers and protects your stomach, especially with the tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see Dr. Patel in two weeks. We’ll check your weight, the tube site, and how you’re doing overall."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel like I’m finally on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You are. You’ve made excellent progress—off TPN, on full feeds, and tolerating food. We’re proud of how far you’ve come."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m just glad I can start healing at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll do great. Call us if you have fever over 101.5, severe pain, or vomiting. Otherwise, rest and let the feeds do their job."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2170-01-19 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. Safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2170-01-19 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick update—your discharge orders are in. Home health nurse will start tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2170-01-19 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. I’ll be ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2170-01-19 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll also send the feeding pump and supplies with you. You’re all set."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2170-01-19 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can’t believe this chapter is over. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2170-01-19 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve worked hard. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2170-01-19 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check before discharge. Vital signs are stable—temperature normal, heart rate down from admission."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2170-01-19 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel stronger already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2170-01-19 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Abdomen is soft, no tenderness. G-tube site looks clean. You’re medically ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2170-01-19 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready. Just need the paperwork and I’ll head out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2170-01-19 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s being printed now. Safe journey home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2170-01-16 03:45:00",
    "admission_end": "2170-01-19 15:14:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for persistent nausea and poor oral intake following gastric bypass surgery, leading to malnutrition and dependence on total parenteral nutrition (TPN). She underwent a laparoscopic gastrostomy tube placement to establish enteral feeding access. Postoperatively, she tolerated tube feeds well, reached goal nocturnal feeding rates, and was weaned off TPN. Her central line was removed, and she began tolerating a stage V diet. She was discharged home with home nursing support for tube feeds, instructions for G-tube care, and a follow-up plan with her surgeon.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified protein-calorie malnutrition",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Bariatric surgery status"
    ]
  }
}
